/home/server-manager/www/arrayhash/mirror-help.arrayhash.com/public/wp-content/plugins/AGENTS.md:417:- Codex, Claude, and other on-server agents should use `/usr/local/bin/mailpit-agent`. It talks to the localhost API without public credentials and returns stable JSON.
/home/server-manager/www/arrayhash/mirror-help.arrayhash.com/public/wp-content/plugins/AGENTS.md-418-- Useful commands: `mailpit-agent status`, `mailpit-agent list [limit]`, `mailpit-agent latest-id`, `mailpit-agent latest`, `mailpit-agent show <id|latest>`, `mailpit-agent text <id|latest>`, and `mailpit-agent html <id|latest>`.
/home/server-manager/www/arrayhash/mirror-help.arrayhash.com/public/wp-content/plugins/AGENTS.md-419-- For a false-positive-safe test, save the current ID before triggering the email, then wait for a message newer than that ID:
/home/server-manager/www/arrayhash/mirror-help.arrayhash.com/public/wp-content/plugins/AGENTS.md-420-
--
/home/server-manager/www/arrayhash/mirror-help.arrayhash.com/public/wp-content/plugins/AGENTS.md-425-```
/home/server-manager/www/arrayhash/mirror-help.arrayhash.com/public/wp-content/plugins/AGENTS.md-426-
/home/server-manager/www/arrayhash/mirror-help.arrayhash.com/public/wp-content/plugins/AGENTS.md-427-- `wait-new` accepts a previous ID (or `none`), a timeout from 1 through 3,600 seconds, and an optional case-insensitive subject substring. It exits `124` on timeout.
/home/server-manager/www/arrayhash/mirror-help.arrayhash.com/public/wp-content/plugins/AGENTS.md:428:- Direct local API access is available at `http://127.0.0.1:8025/api/v1/`; for example, `curl -fsS http://127.0.0.1:8025/api/v1/info | jq`.
/home/server-manager/www/arrayhash/mirror-help.arrayhash.com/public/wp-content/plugins/AGENTS.md-429-
/home/server-manager/www/arrayhash/mirror-help.arrayhash.com/public/wp-content/plugins/AGENTS.md-430-### Operations And Troubleshooting
/home/server-manager/www/arrayhash/mirror-help.arrayhash.com/public/wp-content/plugins/AGENTS.md-431-
/home/server-manager/www/arrayhash/mirror-help.arrayhash.com/public/wp-content/plugins/AGENTS.md-432-- Service checks: `systemctl status mailpit`, `systemctl is-enabled mailpit`, and `journalctl -u mailpit --since today`.
/home/server-manager/www/arrayhash/mirror-help.arrayhash.com/public/wp-content/plugins/AGENTS.md-433-- After changing the Mailpit unit, run `systemctl daemon-reload` and `systemctl restart mailpit`, then verify with `mailpit-agent status`.
/home/server-manager/www/arrayhash/mirror-help.arrayhash.com/public/wp-content/plugins/AGENTS.md-434-- After changing the Caddy site, run `caddy validate --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile` before `systemctl reload caddy`.
/home/server-manager/www/arrayhash/mirror-help.arrayhash.com/public/wp-content/plugins/AGENTS.md:435:- A healthy public endpoint returns `401` without HTTP Basic Authentication and `200` after authentication. A healthy local API returns JSON from `/api/v1/info`.
/home/server-manager/www/arrayhash/mirror-help.arrayhash.com/public/wp-content/plugins/AGENTS.md-436-- Every WP-CLI email test in this workspace must use the documented WordPress path and `--allow-root`.
/home/server-manager/www/arrayhash/mirror-help.arrayhash.com/public/wp-content/plugins/AGENTS.md-437-- Never expose ports `1025` or `8025`, commit the public UI credentials, or forward/release captured messages unless the user explicitly asks.
/home/server-manager/www/arrayhash/mirror-help.arrayhash.com/public/wp-content/plugins/AGENTS.md-438-
